(text "Notes" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 202.2 29.8 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e54caa8f-7092-5e55-b31d-8c65a3dbd1a0"))
(text "Main current path" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 202.2 36.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "77412226-337e-5d55-8a71-788c331cb606"))
(text "BT1 + -> F1 40 A -> J1 -> K1 stud A -> K1 stud B\n-> TB2 -> B+ of U10-U14 (10 AWG).\nB- of U10-U14 -> TB1 star -> J1 -> BT1 -.\nThe blade fuse block carries only the small\nbranches; it is not in the 40 A path.\nK1 precharge: decide after the bench test\n(5 x 470 µF behind a 125 A contactor)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 202.2 39.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "77935345-2ded-5a4b-857d-ae6dd4f3b055"))
(text "Fuse rule" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 202.2 60.58 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a7053a89-9995-55e2-80a1-5e4dcb808de8"))
(text "Every fuse protects the wire after it:\nthe wire is rated above the fuse.\nF1 40 A: 10 AWG. F2 15 A: 14 AWG.\nF6 10 A: 16 AWG. F3-F5, F7, F8: 20 AWG\nor heavier. See WIRE_LIST.md." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 202.2 63.58 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1e3cb77a-8d9c-5762-8697-2add137b11c2"))
